<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Maurice, Landgrave of Hesse-Kassel</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1572–1632</span> · Also known as Maurice the Learned</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Maurice the Learned was Landgrave of Hesse-<a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kassel">Kassel</a> from 1592 to 1627. A scholar, composer and patron of the arts, he founded a court school, supported Heinrich Schütz and built the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ottoneum">Ottoneum</a> in Kassel, the first permanent <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/theatre">theatre</a> in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/germany">Germany</a>. He introduced <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/calvinism">Calvinism</a> to his lands, and losses in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/thirty-tyrants">the Thirty</a> Years' War led him to abdicate in 1627.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/maurice-landgrave-of-hesse-kassel.jpg" alt="Maurice, Landgrave of Hesse-Kassel" width="320" height="553" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Christoph Jobst · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Portr%C3%A4t_des_Landgrafen_Moritz_von_Hessen-Kassel_(1572-1632).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
